(:grammar :name aslSyntax :version "1.0.0" :date "2026-10-08" :start file :generationStart genFile :wordBoundary atomChar
  :d "The single machine-readable grammar of ASL source at the syntax level: what asl-host check accepts before any name, type or arity question. asl/packages/asl-grammar recognizes text with it and generates the other grammars (GBNF for llama.cpp and Ollama today; Lark and tree-sitter later) from it."
  :sources ((:src "asl/host/src/reader.c" :symbols (skipWs isDelim classifyNumber atom escape string datum readSource) :level "bytes, atoms, strings, brackets, column-0 items")
            (:src "asl/host/src/resolve.c" :symbols (declareModule header fnSignature declareEnum declareSchema declareListEnum declareListSchema ctorFields) :level "item shapes: ERR_UNSUPPORTED_TOPLEVEL, ERR_BAD_DEFINITION, ERR_BAD_IMPORT")
            (:src "asl/grammar/v04.asn" :level "history; each :today line there agrees with the rules here"))
  :verdict "Accepting means asl-host check reports none of ERR_READ_UNBALANCED, ERR_BAD_ESCAPE, ERR_READ_NUMBER, ERR_READ_FIELD, ERR_READ_COMMENT, ERR_READ_DOC, ERR_UNSUPPORTED_TOPLEVEL, ERR_BAD_DEFINITION, ERR_BAD_IMPORT for the file itself. Every other diagnostic (unknown symbol, arity, types, effects, let and lambda shapes, duplicate names) is semantic and outside this grammar."
  :notation "A rule is (:rule name expr :d doc). In expr a bare symbol names a rule, a string is a literal, and the forms are (seq e ...) sequence, (alt e ...) ordered choice, (star e) (plus e) (opt e) repetition, (rep e least most) e greedily least to most times, (not e) and (and e) lookahead without consuming, (word s) the literal s not followed by a :wordBoundary byte, (except e "w" ...) what e matches unless that text is one of the words, (cls s) and (ncls s) a byte in or not in s, where a-z inside s is a range, and (end) the end of input. The recognizer reads it as a PEG over bytes."
  :layout "One item per column-0 token, as the host reader groups them: a token outside brackets that starts a line (column 0) opens a new item, and every other token joins the current one. So fn bodies are not indentation-scoped: any indent of at least one byte continues the item, and blank or comment lines between body lines change nothing. The rule gap is the whitespace allowed between tokens of one item at bracket depth 0: a newline run there must be followed by a space, tab, carriage return, comma or comment before the next token. itemBreak is gap followed by newlines, after which the next token sits in column 0. Inside brackets layout is free (ws). The first item may start in any column. Because the rule is a plain context-free condition on newline runs, a GBNF grammar constrains it exactly."
  :approximation "GBNF has no lookahead, so the generated GBNF drops (not e) and (and e) and reads ordered choice and greedy repetition as context-free union and repetition. Its language therefore contains every text the recognizer accepts; it is exact on brackets, strings, escapes, numbers, keywords and layout, and wider where a not excludes words: reserved list heads at top level, the number/keyword exclusion in symbol, and atom boundaries after words."
  :generation "genFile is the start rule for constrained decoding: a canonical subset of file (module header first, list-form schema and enum, fn name a: T -> R on one line with indented body lines, single-space separators, let, fn lambda, mt, cond and if shapes, call heads that are never special-form words, types from Int64 Float64 Bool String Bytes and capitalised names, (List T) (Option T) (Result T E) (Map K V) (Pair A B) at their arity, (fn [A ...] -> R) and user types applied to 1 to 4 types). Its GBNF exclusion of special words is exact: (except r ...) becomes a trie of names. asl-host run asl/packages/asl-grammar/src/gbnf.asl writes hostExact.gbnf and generation.gbnf to ~/.asl/run/grammar (generated, not tracked). Termination contract: the grammar stays unbounded, since no repetition bound that keeps the corpus share also fits max_tokens; a caller whose generation ends with finish_reason length keeps peg/grammarSalvage of it, the longest prefix of whole column-0 items genFile accepts (asl-host run asl/packages/asl-grammar/src/salvage.asl in out). grammarGenerationTest checks corpus share, soundness on sampled texts, and that every gen rule is load-bearing."
  :limits "Two reader checks are not modelled: a float literal of 512 or more bytes (ERR_READ_NUMBER from floatParse) and integer range, which the reader accepts and the compiler rejects."
  :rules [
    (:rule file (seq ws (opt (seq item (star (seq itemBreak item)))) ws (end))
      :d "A file: items separated by column-0 breaks, any whitespace around them. An empty file is valid.")
    (:rule item (alt moduleItem fnItem enumItem schemaItem exprItem)
      :d "One column-0 group. The alternatives are disjoint on the first token.")

    (:rule moduleItem moduleHeader :d "A group of exactly one (module ...) form.")
    (:rule moduleHeader (seq "(" ws (word "module") (opt (seq ws datum headerTail)) ws ")")
      :d "(module path :x [exports] :i [imports]); keys pair left to right from the third element.")
    (:rule headerTail (seq (star (seq ws headerPair)) (opt (seq ws keyword)))
      :d "Key and value pairs, a non-keyword element skipped, and a final lone keyword ignored, as header() steps.")
    (:rule headerPair (seq (not retiredDoc) (alt (seq importsKey ws importList) (seq importsKey ws (alt record string atom)) (seq otherKeyword ws datum) (seq (not keyword) datum)))
      :d "Only :i with a vector or list value is checked; any other value of :i is ignored.")
    (:rule importsKey (word ":i") :d "The imports key.")
    (:rule otherKeyword (seq ":" (alt (seq (ncls "i \t\r\n()[]{}\";,") (star atomChar)) (seq "i" (plus atomChar))))
      :d "A keyword other than :i.")
    (:rule importList (alt (seq "[" ws (star (seq importEntry ws)) "]") (seq "(" ws (star (seq importEntry ws)) ")"))
      :d "The :i value; every entry must name a module.")
    (:rule importEntry (alt symbol (seq "(" ws symbol ws (star (seq datum ws)) ")"))
      :d "path or (path :a alias); anything else is ERR_BAD_IMPORT.")

    (:rule fnItem (seq (word "fn") gap (star (seq fnModifier gap)) defName (star (seq gap (not retiredDoc) datum)))
      :d "fn [! | tailrec | :tailrec]* name, then the header and body tokens. The host reads name: Type pairs and -> Type up to the first non-symbol, and every remaining token as body, so no further shape is a syntax error.")
    (:rule fnModifier (alt (word "!") (word "tailrec") (word ":tailrec")) :d "Effect mark and tail-recursion contract before the name.")
    (:rule enumItem (seq (word "enum") gap defName (star (seq gap datum)))
      :d "enum Name then constructors; the host skips constructor tokens it cannot read.")
    (:rule schemaItem (seq (word "schema") gap defName (star (seq gap datum)))
      :d "schema Name then name: Type field tokens.")
    (:rule exprItem (seq topDatum (star (seq gap topDatum)))
      :d "Any other group: data and forms only. A symbol at depth 0 is ERR_UNSUPPORTED_TOPLEVEL.")
    (:rule topDatum (alt listSchema listEnum plainTopList vector record string number keyword)
      :d "A depth-0 element of an expression group.")
    (:rule plainTopList (seq (not reservedHead) list)
      :d "A top-level form whose head is not a definition word.")
    (:rule reservedHead (seq "(" ws (alt (word "def") (word "defn") (word "defun") (word "df") (word "dfs") (word "defenum") (word "defschema") (word "fn") (word "module") (word "schema") (word "enum")))
      :d "List heads the host rejects at top level (schema and enum only in their exact shapes).")
    (:rule listSchema (seq "(" ws (word "schema") ws defName ws (not retiredDoc) (star (seq schemaField ws)) ")")
      :d "(schema Name (:f field Type \"doc\") ...).")
    (:rule schemaField (alt (seq "(" ws keyword ws defName ws (star (seq datum ws)) ")") string keyword)
      :d "A field form (:key name ...), or a doc string or keyword between fields.")
    (:rule listEnum (seq "(" ws (word "enum") ws defName ws (plus (seq enumVariant ws)) ")")
      :d "(enum Name (:c ctor [params] \"doc\") ...), at least one constructor.")
    (:rule enumVariant (seq "(" ws (word ":c") ws defName ws ctorParams ws (opt (seq string ws)) ")")
      :d "(:c name [params]) with an optional doc string.")
    (:rule ctorParams (seq "[" ws (alt (plus (seq ctorPair ws)) (star (seq symbol ws symbol ws))) "]")
      :d "[(name Type) ...] or the flat [name Type ...], not mixed.")
    (:rule ctorPair (seq "(" ws symbol ws datum ws ")") :d "One (name Type) constructor field.")

    (:rule datum (alt list vector record string atom) :d "Any form.")
    (:rule list (seq "(" ws (star (seq datum ws)) ")" postfix) :d "A parenthesised form, maybe followed by a field chain: (f x).a.b reads as (.-b (.-a (f x))).")
    (:rule postfix (alt (seq fieldChain (not atomChar)) (not (seq "." fieldStart)))
      :d "After ')' a dot and a field start begin a field chain that must run to the next delimiter; anything else there is ERR_READ_FIELD.")
    (:rule fieldChain (plus (seq "." fieldStart (star fieldChar))) :d "One or more .name steps.")
    (:rule fieldStart (cls "a-zA-Z_") :d "The first byte of a field name.")
    (:rule fieldChar (cls "a-zA-Z0-9_?!-") :d "A later byte of a field name.")
    (:rule defName (seq (not dottedName) symbol) :d "A defined name: a symbol the reader keeps whole, never a field chain.")
    (:rule dottedName (seq fieldStart (star (cls "a-zA-Z0-9_?!/-")) fieldChain (not atomChar))
      :d "name.field or alias/name.f.g, which the reader turns into a field access.")
    (:rule vector (seq "[" ws (star (seq datum ws)) "]") :d "A bracketed vector.")
    (:rule record (seq "{" ws (star (seq datum ws)) "}") :d "A braced record.")
    (:rule atom (seq (not oldField) (plus atomChar)) :d "A run of non-delimiter bytes: number, keyword or symbol.")
    (:rule oldField (seq ".-" atomChar) :d "The retired accessor spelling .-f, ERR_READ_FIELD: write x.f or (expr).f.")
    (:rule atomChar (ncls " \t\r\n()[]{}\";,") :d "Any byte that is not a delimiter; bytes from 0x80 are atom bytes.")
    (:rule number (seq (opt (cls "+-")) (plus digit) (opt (seq "." (plus digit))) (opt (seq (cls "eE") (opt (cls "+-")) (plus digit))) (not atomChar))
      :d "classifyNumber: the whole atom is a decimal integer or float. .5 and 1. are symbols.")
    (:rule keyword (seq ":" (plus atomChar)) :d "A colon and at least one more byte; a lone : is a symbol.")
    (:rule symbol (seq (not number) (not keyword) (not oldField) (plus atomChar)) :d "An atom that is neither a number nor a keyword.")
    (:rule digit (cls "0-9") :d "A decimal digit.")

    (:rule string (seq "\"" (star (alt escape (ncls "\"\\"))) "\"") :d "A string; raw newlines are allowed.")
    (:rule escape (seq "\\" (alt (cls "ntr\\\"") (seq "x" hex hex) (seq "u{" bracedScalar) (seq "u" hex4Scalar)))
      :d "\\n \\t \\r \\\\ \\\" \\xHH \\uXXXX \\u{1 to 6 hex}; anything else is ERR_BAD_ESCAPE.")
    (:rule hex (cls "0-9a-fA-F") :d "A hex digit.")
    (:rule hex4Scalar (alt (seq (cls "0-9a-cA-Ce-fE-F") hex hex hex) (seq (cls "dD") (cls "0-7") hex hex))
      :d "Four hex digits that are not a surrogate (D800 to DFFF).")
    (:rule bracedScalar (alt (seq "00" hex4Scalar "}") (seq "0" (cls "1-9a-fA-F") hex hex hex hex "}") (seq "10" hex hex hex hex "}")
                             (seq "0" hex4Scalar "}") (seq (cls "1-9a-fA-F") hex hex hex hex "}")
                             (seq hex4Scalar "}") (seq hex hex hex "}") (seq hex hex "}") (seq hex "}"))
      :d "1 to 6 hex digits and the closing brace, a scalar value: at most 10FFFF and not a surrogate.")

    (:rule ws (star (alt space newline comment)) :d "Whitespace inside brackets and around items.")
    (:rule gap (star (alt space comment (seq (plus newline) (alt space comment))))
      :d "Whitespace between depth-0 tokens of one item: a newline run continues the item only when a space or comment follows it.")
    (:rule itemBreak (seq gap (plus newline)) :d "The end of an item: the next token starts a line.")
    (:rule space (cls " \t\r,") :d "Blank bytes; a comma is whitespace.")
    (:rule newline "\n" :d "A line feed; a carriage return is a blank byte.")
    (:rule comment (seq ";" (star (cls "; \t")) "(:m" (not wordByte) (star (seq (not whyKey) (ncls "\n"))))
      :d "A comment is one (:m ...) meta form to the end of the line, without :why; free comments are ERR_READ_COMMENT, their text lives in doc.asn.")
    (:rule whyKey (seq ":why" (not wordByte)) :d "The retired :why key of a meta comment.")
    (:rule wordByte (cls "a-zA-Z0-9_?!-") :d "A byte that continues a word.")
    (:rule retiredDoc (seq (alt (word ":d") (word ":doc")) ws string) :d "A :d or :doc docstring in a module, fn or list-form schema header, ERR_READ_DOC: its text lives in doc.asn.")

    (:rule genFile (seq genModule (star (seq genItemBreak genItem)) (star "\n") (end))
      :d "Generation start: the canonical subset a model is constrained to. A module header first, then column-0 items separated by line feeds. Every text it derives, read as a context-free grammar (lookahead dropped, as in GBNF), is free of the syntax-level diagnostics in :verdict; grammarGenerationTest samples it to check that.")
    (:rule genItemBreak (plus "\n") :d "One or more line feeds; the next item starts in column 0.")
    (:rule genItem (alt genFn genSchema genEnum genComment) :d "A canonical item: fn, list-form schema, list-form enum, or a comment line.")
    (:rule genComment (seq "; (:m " (star (seq (not ":why") (ncls "\n")))) :d "A meta comment line, such as ; (:m :tags (io)).")
    (:rule genModule (seq "(module " genWordName (opt (seq genSep genHeaderExports)) (opt (seq genSep genHeaderImports)) ")")
      :d "(module path :x [names] :i [imports]): each key at most once, in this order, so a model cannot loop on header keys.")
    (:rule genHeaderExports (seq ":x [" (opt (seq genWordName (star (seq genSep genWordName)))) "]") :d "Exported names.")
    (:rule genHeaderImports (seq ":i [" (opt (seq genImport (star (seq genSep genImport)))) "]") :d "Imports.")
    (:rule genImport (alt genWordName (seq "(" genWordName " :a " genWordName ")")) :d "path or (path :a alias).")
    (:rule genFn (seq "fn " (opt (alt "! " "tailrec ")) genDefName (star (seq " " genParam)) " -> " genType (plus (seq genLineBreak genBodyElem)))
      :d "fn name a: T ... -> R on one line, then indented body lines.")
    (:rule genParam (seq genWordName ": " genType) :d "A typed parameter.")
    (:rule genBodyElem genExpr :d "A body line: an expression; docs live in doc.asn.")
    (:rule genLineBreak (seq "\n" (star (seq (star " ") (opt genComment) "\n")) (plus " "))
      :d "A line feed, any blank or comment lines, then an indent of at least one space, so the next token is never in column 0.")
    (:rule genSep (alt " " genLineBreak) :d "Separator between elements: one space or one indented line break, so a model cannot pad with blanks.")
    (:rule genSchema (seq "(schema " genDefName (star (seq genSep genField)) ")") :d "(schema Name (:f field Type \"doc\") ...).")
    (:rule genField (seq "(:f " genDefName " " genType (opt (seq " " string)) (opt (seq " :default " genExpr)) ")") :d "A schema field.")
    (:rule genEnum (seq "(enum " genDefName (plus (seq genSep genVariant)) ")") :d "(enum Name (:c ctor [(field Type)] \"doc\") ...).")
    (:rule genVariant (seq "(:c " genDefName " [" (opt (seq genCtorField (star (seq " " genCtorField)))) "]" (opt (seq " " string)) ")") :d "An enum constructor.")
    (:rule genCtorField (seq "(" genDefName " " genType ")") :d "A constructor field (name Type).")
    (:rule genType (alt genTypeApp genTypeName) :d "A type: a named type or an applied one.")
    (:rule genTypeApp (alt (seq "(List " genType ")") (seq "(Option " genType ")") (seq "(Result " genType " " genType ")") (seq "(Map " genType " " genType ")") (seq "(Pair " genType " " genType ")") genFnType (seq "(" genTypeCtor (rep (seq " " genType) 1 4) ")"))
      :d "(List T) (Option T) (Result T E) (Map K V) (Pair A B) with their arity, a fn type, or a user type applied to 1 to 4 types.")
    (:rule genFnType (seq (alt "(fn [" "(Fn [") (opt (seq genType (rep (seq " " genType) 0 7))) "] -> " genType ")") :d "(fn [A B] -> R); types.c parseType reads Fn as fn.")
    (:rule genTypeName (alt (seq genTypeAlias "/" genUpperName) genUpperName) :d "Int64, Float64, Bool, String, Bytes or any capitalised type, maybe behind an import alias: ty/SsaModule.")
    (:rule genTypeCtor (alt (seq genTypeAlias "/" genUpperName) genUserType) :d "A user type constructor; the builtin ones keep their own arity.")
    (:rule genUserType (except genUpperName "List" "Option" "Result" "Map" "Pair") :d "A capitalised name other than a builtin type constructor.")
    (:rule genTypeAlias (seq (cls "a-z") (rep (cls "a-zA-Z0-9_-") 0 79)) :d "An import alias before / in a type.")
    (:rule genUpperName (seq (cls "A-Z") (rep (cls "a-zA-Z0-9_") 0 79)) :d "A capitalised type name.")

    (:rule genExpr (alt genLet genLambda genMatch genCond genIf genWith genCall genVector genRecord string genAtom) :d "A canonical expression.")
    (:rule genLet (seq "(let [" (opt genBindings) "]" (plus (seq genSep genExpr)) ")") :d "(let [(name value) ...] body ...); the flat [name value ...] form is accepted too.")
    (:rule genBindings (alt (seq genBinding (star (seq genSep genBinding))) (seq genWordName genSep genExpr (star (seq genSep genWordName genSep genExpr))))
      :d "Binding pairs or a flat name value list.")
    (:rule genBinding (seq "(" genWordName genSep genExpr ")") :d "(name value).")
    (:rule genLambda (seq "(fn [" (opt (seq genLambdaParam (star (seq " " genLambdaParam)))) "]" (opt (seq " -> " genType)) (plus (seq genSep genExpr)) ")")
      :d "(fn [(x T) ...] -> R body).")
    (:rule genLambdaParam (alt (seq "(" genWordName " " genType ")") genWordName) :d "A lambda parameter, typed or bare.")
    (:rule genMatch (seq "(" (alt "mt" "match") genSep genExpr (plus (seq genSep genArm)) ")") :d "(mt subject (pattern body) ...).")
    (:rule genArm (seq "(" genPattern (plus (seq genSep genExpr)) ")") :d "A match arm.")
    (:rule genPattern (alt (seq "(" genName (star (seq " " genName)) ")") number string genName) :d "(ctor binders), a literal, a binder, _ or else.")
    (:rule genCond (seq "(cond" (plus (seq genSep genClause)) ")") :d "(cond (test body) ... (else body)).")
    (:rule genClause (seq "(" genExpr (plus (seq genSep genExpr)) ")") :d "A cond clause.")
    (:rule genIf (seq "(if" genSep genExpr genSep genExpr genSep genExpr ")") :d "(if test then else).")
    (:rule genCall (alt "()" (seq "(" genHead (star (seq genSep genExpr)) ")" (opt genFields))) :d "A call, maybe followed by a field chain; its head is never a special-form word.")
    (:rule genWith (seq "(with " genExpr (plus (seq genSep genKeyword genSep genExpr)) ")") :d "(with record :field value ...), a copy with the named fields replaced.")
    (:rule genFields (plus (seq "." genFieldName)) :d "A field chain .a.b after a name or a call.")
    (:rule genFieldName (seq (cls "a-zA-Z_") (rep (cls "a-zA-Z0-9_?!") 0 79)) :d "A field name of at most 80 bytes.")
    (:rule genHead (alt genPlainName genOpName genLambda genCall) :d "A call head: a name other than let fn mt match cond if, an operator, a lambda or a call.")
    (:rule genPlainName (except genWordName "let" "fn" "mt" "match" "cond" "if" "with") :d "A word name that is not a special-form head.")
    (:rule genVector (seq "[" (opt (seq genExpr (star (seq genSep genExpr)))) "]") :d "A vector.")
    (:rule genRecord (seq "{" (opt (seq genExpr (star (seq genSep genExpr)))) "}") :d "A record.")
    (:rule genAtom (alt number genKeyword (seq genWordName (opt genFields)) genOpName) :d "A number, keyword, name with an optional field chain, or operator.")
    (:rule genKeyword (seq ":" genKeywordName) :d "A keyword other than :d, so a keyword and a string can never form a retired docstring.")
    (:rule genKeywordName (except genWordName "d") :d "A keyword word other than d.")
    (:rule genName (alt genWordName genOpName) :d "A symbol that can never read as a number or keyword.")
    (:rule genWordName (seq (cls "a-zA-Z_") (rep (cls "a-zA-Z0-9_.?!/*'<>=+-") 0 79)) :d "A word name of at most 80 bytes, so a model cannot spin inside one: camelCase, a/b paths, a.b field chains, names ending in ? or !.")
    (:rule genDefName (seq (cls "a-zA-Z_") (rep (cls "a-zA-Z0-9_?!/*'<>=+-") 0 79)) :d "A defined name: a word name without dots, so the reader never reads it as a field access.")
    (:rule genOpName (seq (cls "+*/<>=!%-") (rep (cls "+*/<>=!%-") 0 3)) :d "An operator name: + - * / < > = <= -> != with no digits, so never a number.")
  ])
